WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.540
Yeah, I'm gonna come back

2
00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:02.320
to the point you made

3
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.720
and this comes back to something

4
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.660
I talked about earlier

5
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.520
about how different zone two is

6
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.590
for different people.

7
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:08.520
And you know, like,

8
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.910
you're gonna go out and work out.

9
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.060
You wanna make sure

10
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.470
you're getting a good workout.

11
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.990
And for a lot of people, I think,

12
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.200
especially sedentary people

13
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.750
who are starting to exercise,

14
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.090
zone two would be walking.

15
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.170
And as soon as you start to jog,

16
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.880
that's probably true for me, I imagine,

17
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.090
as soon as I'm jogging, I'm above zone two.

18
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.620
So if you think about it in that context,

19
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.620
if we're actually telling people to go out

20
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.640
and you have 30 minutes to exercise,

21
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.750
but you need to be in zone two,

22
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.950
that means you're just going for a 30-minute walk

23
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.250
as opposed to doing a 30-minute jog.

24
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.980
And I think when you think about it

25
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.790
in that context, it's pretty intuitive that,

26
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.320
well, the benefits are gonna be better

27
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.470
from the jogging, right?

28
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:46.730
Not walking.

29
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.600
And there are benefits from walking for sure,

30
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.530
but you're gonna get more if you jog.

31
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.360
So I think that's an important context

32
00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.740
in recognizing, like for a marathon runner,

33
00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.610
zone two intensity is really fast.

34
00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.410
like they're running,

35
00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.530
but for the average person,

36
00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.010
it could be a walk.
